The patch file
--------------

install/DigiGlide_35.dgpatch
    How to make image 35's MAIN OS section from the stock one: steps that copy a stretch of the user's own stock
    section (an offset and a length, never the bytes) and steps that carry bytes. The carried bytes are: DigiGlide's
    compiled code and data (source: mod/, AGPL-3.0-or-later), dnfw's runtime loader in compiled form (source:
    install/vendor/dnfw_csrc/, AGPL-3.0-or-later), and 494 bytes at the 135 places the build changes in stock
    (calls into DigiGlide, the relocated parameter table's addresses, its 55 raised bounds, the loader). The copy of
    Elektron's parameter table that a built image holds is a copy step. install/make_patch.py makes the file and
    stops if any carried stretch of 16 bytes or more also occurs in the stock section. The file also holds SHA-256
    hashes of the stock file, of its MAIN OS section and of the result.
    The compiled code includes the USB probe (mod/probe.S, see below; its digihealth part is GPL-2.0-or-later, used
    under GPL-3.0, which section 13 of the AGPL allows to be combined) and the port of Brickglide (MIT).

Included from other projects
----------------------------

install/vendor/dnfw/
    25 files copied unchanged from dnfw (angellinares/dn2_firmware_explore, commit 1a9f452), AGPL-3.0-or-later, the
    same licence text as LICENSE: the SysEx transport, the container, the aPLib codec and the integrity code the
    patcher needs to read the stock file and write the image. dnfw ported these from elektron-firmware-tool
    (mischa85, Marcel Bierling), MIT; that notice and the MIT text are in install/vendor/DNFW-THIRD-PARTY.md, dnfw's
    own THIRD-PARTY.md, copied whole.

install/vendor/dnfw_csrc/
    The source of the runtime loader every image contains: dnfw's csrc/runtime/loader.S, unchanged, and
    csrc/include/dn2_111.h with the one address the OS 1.12 build changes (DNFW_AREA, see mod/port_os.py).
    AGPL-3.0-or-later.

Files derived from other projects
---------------------------------

mod/probe.S
    Derived from dnfw (angellinares/dn2_firmware_explore), csrc/usbprobe/probe.S, AGPL-3.0-or-later, which is
    derived from irpina/digihealth (sysinfo.s), GPL-2.0-or-later.

tools/dgprobe.py
    Protocol and codec derived from dnfw, tools/dn2probe.py, AGPL-3.0-or-later, which is derived from
    irpina/digihealth (tools/digiusb.py), GPL-2.0-or-later.

mod/preflight.py
    The rules of dnfw v0.50's safety check, applied to the stock file of the OS being built. Calls dnfw.

port/harness_1.12.patch
    Local changes to two other projects, kept as a patch with a few lines of their context:
    complex-ping/digitone-2-modding-skill, scripts/cfkit.py (MIT), and m-dwyer/digikit,
    devices/digitone-ii.toml (GPL-2.0-or-later).

model/digiglide.py, mod/core/dg_core.c
    The glide planner, voice leading, paths, Moves and tables are a port of Brickglide, part of
    michaeltietjen/brickchord (brickchord/ambient.py, engine.py, main.py), MIT, by the same author.

Used at build or test time, not included (the patcher needs none of these)
----------------------------------------

dnfw (angellinares/dn2_firmware_explore), AGPL-3.0-or-later
    For the build: the code area, the C build, the parameter table relocation (dnfw.patch.paramtable),
    verification. (Its container code and its loader's source are included, see above.) A built DigiGlide image
    contains dnfw code, which is why DigiGlide is AGPL-3.0-or-later.

digitone-2-modding-skill (complex-ping), MIT
    The ColdFire build helpers and the emulator harness the tests drive (cfmod, cfkit, emu).

digikit (m-dwyer), GPL-2.0-or-later, and digiemu (irpina), GPL-2.0-or-later
    The emulators (ColdFire and SHARC) the tests run in.

Read, no code taken
-------------------

naturarum/dn2-cfw (Digiwerk), GPL-2.0-or-later: its notes on the kit record, the kit serializer and the parameter table
(T6.0, T6.3, docs/parameter-table-growth.md) guided where DigiGlide keeps its settings. Addresses and layouts
were checked against the author's own OS 1.12 file and unit.
